    "Forces the internal framebuffer to a low resolution. Stretched modes scale the framebuffer to fill the game viewport. Pixel-perfect modes render N64-native 320x240 and draw it at an integer factor, centred with black borders — sharper retro look, no sub-pixel blur. Auto-fit picks the largest factor that still fits in the window. Overrides Internal Resolution while active. Latched at startup — changes take effect on next launch (toggling mid-session would resize the framebuffer and race the Metal renderer).": "",
